# Zerops .deployignore (gitignore syntax). zcli applies it twice: to the source it uploads for the build, and to the
# deployFiles artefact (./bundle). Directory patterns MUST be anchored with a leading "/": an unanchored
# `node_modules/` also matched bundle/node_modules and bundle/.next/node_modules, so the first deploy shipped a
# 0.6 MiB artefact and server.js died with "Cannot find module 'next'" (docs/notes/deploy.md).
# Secrets stay unanchored on purpose: no .env may ship at any depth.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
/node_modules/
/.next/
/dist/
/bundle/**/.env
/coverage/
/spikes/
/tools/
/research/
/data/calls/
/tests/
/docs/
/.github/
/.vercel/
/.turbo/
/.wt/
